<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hrabanus Maurus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 780–856</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Rabanus Maurus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hrabanus Maurus was a Frankish monk, scholar and theologian, a pupil of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcuin-of-york">Alcuin</a>. As master of the school and then abbot of Fulda from 822 to 842 he made it one of the leading centres of learning in the Carolingian world, earning the title 'teacher of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'. He became archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> in 847 and wrote the encyclopedia De rerum naturis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hrabanus-maurus.jpg" alt="Hrabanus Maurus" width="320" height="341" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fulda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raban-Maur_Alcuin_Otgar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
